ncers over a 5-year period (2007–2011) were calculated for Puerto Rico.\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Annual incidence rates per 100,000 population were age-adjusted by the direct method to the 2000 U.S. standard population using 19 age-categories.\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"When <16 cases were reported, the number and rate are not presented because of the potential for statistically unreliable estimates\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"A variation on this algorithm was used to derive the completeness of case ascertainment in Puerto Rico\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Maps were created using ArcGIS by rank-ordering the Puerto Rico municipalities' incidence rates and then grouping into quartiles.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Incidence rates of selected cancers over a 5-year period (2007–2011) were calculated for Puerto Rico.\"}], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"uncertain_fields\": []}", "type": "text"}]}